<!--
  HueTheme.xaml · shared dark theme for the icon-family app suite
  Pure XAML, .NET 6+. Every app looks the same except for its family colour (= its domain).

  The rules, the style reference and the migration steps are in HUETHEME-HANDOVER.md.
  It is the source of truth; read it before writing any code.

  ADOPTING IT
    1. Copy to Theme/HueTheme.xaml (Build Action: Page) and merge it in App.xaml.
    2. Every window: Style="{StaticResource Hue.Window}" (implicit Window styles skip
       derived windows).
    3. Add HueThemeKit.cs: HueContrast.Follow(this) in App.OnStartup,
       HueTitleBar.Attach(this) in every window's constructor.
    4. Busy overlay: add BusyOverlay/src. It reads its colours (Busy.*) from this file.

  PICKING THE FAMILY
    Edit only the ACTIVE block: the family prefix on the accent lines ("Cyan." -> "Red."),
    "Neutral." or "<Family>.Tint." on the surface lines, Glow.Opacity, and the CONFIGURED
    FOR line.

  PALETTE ROLES (per family)
    Base       the accent: markers, lines, selection bars, focus borders. Never under text.
    Fill       primary-button and checked fill, with OnAccent text. Deeper than Base in
               Indigo, Rose and Red, where the bright hue cannot carry readable text.
    Light      accent text and every glow.
    Pale       busy rings only.
    Soft, SoftHover, Edge   Base at 14 / 24 / 40 % alpha: tonal fills and their borders.
-->
